    "source": "https://github.com/lowRISC/ibex/pull/54",
    "title": "Fix decoding of C.LI, C.LUI, C.SRLI, C.SRAI, C.SSLI",
    "base_commit": "cd15ce88beba8ed8496f414af361f664764f47e2",
    "merge_commit": "5319734180ac4844e43d31ad19dc108aac503037",
    "fix_commits": [
      "687952e42f3eff68348770ae0c55bc5c0f036d3e"
    ],
    "intent": "In the compressed instruction decoder, several RISC-V compressed HINT encodings are being reported as illegal instructions. In the RISC-V C extension, these encodings are legal HINT/no-op forms: `C.LI` with destination register `x0`, `C.LUI` with destination register `x0` and a non-zero immediate (for example `0x7065`), and `C.SRLI`, `C.SRAI`, or `C.SLLI` with shift amount `0`. Ibex currently treats these compressed instructions as illegal instead of recognizing them as valid compressed HINTs. The bug affects `ibex_compressed_decoder` whenever one of those specific HINT forms is presented. The expected behavior is that these instructions are still recognized as compressed instructions and do not raise the illegal-instruction indication.",
